# Skeletal reduction of USC-II with experimental validation of macroscopic observables

Autonomous kinetic-mechanism reduction run.  Everything below was produced inside this
workspace; raw inputs, scripts, failures and source URLs are kept alongside the report.

---

## 0. Summary

* **What is delivered.**  Three skeletal mechanisms that are strict, byte-verified subsets of
  the supplied USC-II mechanism (`deliverable/`): **103 species / 751 reactions**,
  **89 / 671** and **68 / 473**, from 111 species / 784 reactions.  Nothing is re-fitted, so
  every claim is checkable against the parent.
* **How they were chosen.**  A decision rule was written down *before* the experimental
  comparison (section 7.0): confirmation-matrix ignition fidelity `max |ln(tau/tau_parent)|
  <= 0.35`, `rms <= 0.12`, `|dTad| <= 20 K`, and laminar burning velocity within 10 % of the
  parent in every one of 19 fuel families.  Applied mechanically, it selects the
  **103-species** mechanism; the 89- and 68-species mechanisms are delivered as the
  compression and aggressive rungs, each with its measured excess error stated.
* **The measured trade-off** (worst / rms over 314 confirmation conditions; flame = worst
  family of the 19-family archetype curve):

  | | 103 sp | 89 sp | 68 sp |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | ignition, all conditions | 0.179 / 0.018 | 0.487 / 0.040 | 1.678 / 0.118 |
  | ignition, T >= 1100 K (206 conditions) | 0.028 / 0.004 | 0.058 / 0.011 | 0.414 / 0.068 |
  | laminar burning velocity | 1.1 % | 6.7 % | 18.6 % |
  | equilibrium temperature (54 states) | 0.0 K | 0.0 K | 0.0 K |

* **Against experiment** (499 FFCM-2/SFCPD targets with curated uncertainties + 1113 archive
  ignition points, 108 flame-speed points): the reduced mechanisms are statistically
  indistinguishable from the parent up to 88 species (median ln(model/exp) -0.089 parent vs
  -0.090 at 103 species); the 68-species mechanism degrades benzene and ethylene by
  0.3-0.4 log units.  The large disagreements that exist (methanol +1.53, acetylene +1.43,
  ethane -0.65 log units) are **inherited from USC-II unchanged**.
* **What was found that changes how the evidence must be read.**  The SciExpeM archive
  contains seven pairs of byte-identical files with contradictory `ms`/`us` unit
  declarations and a whole benzene series whose `ms` values are physically impossible; after
  correction the archived benzene median moves from -6.66 to -0.46 log units (section 4,
  item 6, and 7.6).  The binding constraints of the reduction are a flame-speed sensitivity (C2H2,
  C3H6, C6H6) and a 900-1100 K aromatic ignition corner that **no measurement in these
  sources reaches**.
* **A measured, not assumed, attribution.**  The flame-speed loss that binds the whole
  trade-off (the 91 -> 88 species step) is caused by a **single species, `iC4H3`**: putting it
  back alone restores the acetylene flame speed to the 91-species value exactly, and the
  89-species mechanism that results dominates both the 88- and the 91-species ones on every
  measured axis (section 7.4).
* **What is not claimed.**  Global optimality; validity below 900 K, above the declared
  pressure range, or for fuels outside the parent's species set; and the usual caveat that
  agreement with the parent is not agreement with nature.  A DRGEP/DRG pre-screen was tried
  first and had no discriminative power on this mechanism (section 5.4) — a negative result
  that is reported rather than hidden.

