Section 7.4 shows the first constraint is physically real (it is a change in a measured
observable), while section 7.6 shows the second one is not currently backed by any
measurement, so a user who is willing to accept unvalidated error in that corner can take
a much smaller mechanism.

For that reason **three mechanisms are delivered instead of one**, ordered by how much of
section 7.0's evidence they are allowed to violate:

1. `mech3/mech_nsp103.yaml` — the rule-compliant mechanism; 103 species / 751 reactions
   (7 % fewer species, 4 % fewer reactions), every criterion of section 7.0 met, agreement
   with experiment identical to the parent's, and elemental/thermodynamic consistency
   verified species-by-species (`results/integrity_deliverable.json`).
2. `deliverable/usc2_skel_089sp_671rx.yaml` — 89 species / 671 reactions (20 % fewer).  This
